OpenSSL FIPS support


1. Overview

The OpenSSL 3.x includes a cryptographic module that can be FIPS validated.
The module is implemented as an OpenSSL provider. A provider is essentially
a dynamically loadable module which implements cryptographic algorithms.

See https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/master/README-FIPS.md for further
details.


2. Enable FIPS Mode in Kernel

The 'fips=1' option needs to be added to the kernel command line so that key
generation is done with FIPS approved algorithms:
